// Two tail lambdas keep their `return`, and the checker refuses each one.
//
// The checker reads a bare tail lambda as a returned box only where the
// expected type returns a box of a function. Elsewhere the lambda stays a
// computation, and its body needs the `return`.
//
// A box of a computation that is no function has no lambda to read. The
// checker refuses that lambda with `ShapeMismatch`. A definition that states
// no type has no box to read. The checker refuses its lambda with
// `NotSynthesisable`.
//
// - see: #6390

/// Two values.
data Two : Type where
  /// The left value.
  | Left : Two
  /// The right value.
  | Right : Two

/// A box of a computation that is no function.
@[refuses("ShapeMismatch")]
def no_function() -> () -> Two =
  fun (u) {
    u
  }

/// The definition states no type.
@[refuses("NotSynthesisable")]
def unstated = fun (u) { u };
